# Local environment for the frontend on the host, per ADR-0400 and ADR-0205.
# `mise run dev:frontend` sets both vars below. You need this file only if you start `next dev` another way, such as an IDE run config or a debugger.
# Copy it to .env.local. Next loads it before it evaluates next.config.mjs.
#
# Prerequisites. The edge, Kratos, and the services all run in the cluster:
#   mise run cluster:up -- full    # once: the full local platform
#   then register or log in at https://dev.localtest.me:8443/auth/register

# The environment's edge origin. It is the single URL that configures this app.
#   • Server components fetch through it, in src/lib/server-fetch/server.ts. The /api/<resource> IngressRoutes match on Host(dev.localtest.me), and Oathkeeper injects identity there.
#     So requests go to the edge, never to a service or a cluster-internal address. If it is unset, /panel/products throws on its first fetch.
#   • next.config.mjs derives the server-action CSRF allowlist from it.
# Browser-side calls need nothing: client.ts uses a relative /api, per ADR-0306.
EDGE_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://dev.localtest.me:8443

# Local only. The wildcard cert comes from the SelfSigned ClusterIssuer. It is a self-signed leaf, not a CA, so NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS cannot make Node trust it.
# Without this, the server-side fetch above fails the handshake.
# Deployed envs have Let's Encrypt certs and set neither this nor a CA bundle.
NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0

# Build identity, per ADR-0103. CI passes the git SHA or release. Locally, the `dev` defaults in next.config.mjs are fine.
# SERVICE_VERSION=dev
# DEPLOY_ENV=dev

# Browser RUM beacons, per ADR-0500. With the full tier up and `mise run dev:forward` running, uncomment this to forward Faro beacons to the cluster's OTel Collector.
# If it is unset, the dev-only /api/rum handler returns 204 and drops them.
# FARO_COLLECT_URL=http://localhost:12347/collect

# Fixture mode, per ADR-0701. Uncomment it to serve every seam in src/lib/data/ from its committed fixture and not from the service.
# This lets you design a screen before its API exists. On a preview deployment, it makes the app a clickable demo.
# A production build with this set fails during prerender, on purpose.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIXTURES=1
